utions worldwide. The company offers Mobile Deposit, a mobile remote deposit capture solution for retail financial institutions, brokerages, and prepaid card providers; Check Fraud Defender, a cloud-hosted fraud mitigation service; Mitek Verified Identity Platform, an end-to-end identity verification solution; Mobile Verify, an omnichannel identity document verification engine; MiSnap, a software development kit that replaces manual image capture with auto-capture; CheckReader, which enables financial institutions to automatically extract data from checks once they have been scanned or photographed by the application; and Check Intelligence, a check fraud solution. It also provides IDLive Face, a passive face liveness detection; IDLive Doc, a document liveness detection; and IDLive Voice, an anti-spoofing voice liveness. The company was incorporated in 1986 and is based in San Diego, California.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Edward H. West | CEO & Director | Age 58 | Compensation: $1.5M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 561 people. Revenue per employee of $320K ranks in the below the sector median among Technology peers, with revenue growing 23%/yr across its filed history. Each employee generates $97K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $30K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 5\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags moderate compensation governance risk (6/10).","financial_summary":["Mitek Systems, Inc. is a small-cap technology business with a $819M market cap on $180M of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +8% over the past three years and +22% annually across the full decade, a respectable pace for a business of this size.","Returns on capital run at 18% against a 10% cost of capital \u2014 a 8-point spread that is the clearest signature of an economic moat.","The business throws off $54M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 30 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 6.29\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, the balance sheet carries net cash, which is the gold standard: the business never has to make desperate decisions in a bad year, and thin 1.7\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Shareholder yield is only 0.6%, a thin return of capital, and insiders hold 3.5% of the shares, and profit capture is only 0.4\u00d7 the fair share, suggesting no structural edge inside its industry."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Low reinvestment-driven growth suggests the compounding engine has stalled","sev":"amber","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Piotroski score 4/9 \u2014 below the median for a healthy business","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Altman Z in the grey zone \u2014 financial health warrants monitoring","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Above-average short interest at 9.7% of float","sev":"amber","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Significant insider selling (net $2.4M)","sev":"amber","cat":"insider","dollars":-2422726.2},{"text":"Technology sector lagging the market significantly, underperforming by 7% over 3 months","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Elevated sector volatility (38% annualized) adds uncertainty","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Antitrust and platform-regulation risk \u2014 the larger the network effect, the larger the regulatory target on its back, and a single consent decree can reset the moat.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Cybersecurity liability and talent cost inflation \u2014 a single breach can erase years of goodwill, and the war for engineering talent compresses margins even at scale.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Shares offer a 25% margin of safety against estimated fair value","Market is pricing in lower growth than the company has historically delivered","Among the least levered in Technology \u2014 the fortress balance sheet in its peer set"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Price-Driven Insight from (MITK) for Rule-Based Strategy","source":"news.stocktradersdaily.com","link":"https://news.stocktradersdaily.com/news_release/43/Price-Driven_Insight_from_MITK_for_Rule-Based_Strategy_111226125001_1794505801.html","date":"2026-11-12","timestamp":1794505801.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.0,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Mitek Systems (NASDAQ:MITK) Stock Breaks Above Fifty Day Moving Average \u2013 What\u2019s Next?","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/10/mitek-systems-nasdaqmitk-stock-breaks-above-fifty-day-moving-average-whats-next.html","date":"2026-11-10","timestamp":1794307042.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.836,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Understanding Momentum Shifts in (MITK)","source":"news.stocktradersdaily.com","link":"https://news.stocktradersdaily.com/news_release/91/Understanding_Momentum_Shifts_in_MITK_110226010201_1793642522.html","date":"2026-11-02","timestamp":1793642522.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.0,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Mitek Systems, Inc. $MITK Holdings Cut by Skylands Capital LLC","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/10/22/mitek-systems-inc-mitk-holdings-cut-by-skylands-capital-llc.html","date":"2026-10-22","timestamp":1792662445.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.827,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Mitek Systems (NASDAQ:MITK) Stock Breaks Above 200 Day Moving Average \u2013 Here\u2019s What Happened","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/10/17/mitek-systems-nasdaqmitk-stock-breaks-above-200-day-moving-average-heres-what-happened.html","date":"2026-10-17","timestamp":1792273266.0,"o